00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:46.930
but you have to
convert your model

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:49.640
from one format
to another format,

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:52.814
and then do validation on
it, that type of thing.

00:14:52.814 --> 00:14:54.230
There's some
technical challenges.

00:14:54.230 --> 00:14:57.640
Somebody mentioned that just
creating a serving system

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:00.490
is a very complex stack.

00:15:00.490 --> 00:15:01.840
You have your load balancing.

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:02.620
You have your web server.

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:03.610
You have authentication.

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:04.500
You have authorization.

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:05.666
Oftentimes you have a cache.

00:15:05.666 --> 00:15:06.700
You have logging agents.

00:15:06.700 --> 00:15:07.940
You have monitoring agents.

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:10.510
They all have to work together.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.550
One thing is to get
all of those up.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:14.920
Another thing is to keep
all of them up, right?

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:17.470
Because if any one of
those pieces goes down,

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:19.130
it's your pager that goes off.

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:21.239
If you're the
production engineer.

00:15:21.239 --> 00:15:23.030
And you probably don't
want that to happen.

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:25.510
And certainly, those of you
that are data scientists,

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:27.160
even if you're
capable of doing this,

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:29.535
that's probably the last thing
on earth you'd want to do.

00:15:29.535 --> 00:15:32.260
Otherwise, you would be a
production engineer and not

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:33.910
a data scientist.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:36.880
So here's what Cloud ML
Engine Prediction offers.

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:38.460
It's click-to-deploy.

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:42.070
It has horizontal auto-scaling,
so as you send out

00:15:42.070 --> 00:15:43.330
more traffic, it scales up.

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:44.740
You send out less
traffic, it scales down.

00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:46.823
And it's serverless, so
it scales all the way down

00:15:46.823 --> 00:15:50.720
to zero, which is really
fantastic when, say, you're

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:52.870
a startup, and your
traffic patterns

00:15:52.870 --> 00:15:55.090
are very sparse at
the beginning phases.

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:56.920
You get some traffic
and you're happy.

00:15:56.920 --> 00:15:59.110
It scales down really low
and you're not so happy.

00:15:59.110 --> 00:16:00.820
Or very spiky traffic.

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:02.680
We scale up very quickly.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:06.850
Our servers are able to scale
very world-class, really.

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:09.880
We give you encryption,
authentication, authorization,

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:11.410
logging, monitoring.

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:13.420
You can organize your
models with labels.

00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:16.460
You can do versioning rollouts
and things of that nature.

